    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 133,
      "bottomRightX": 434,
      "bottomRightY": 151,
      "content": "Thus $u_{nn'}^{(r)}$ is a homogeneous polynomial of the $r$th order in $\\zeta_i$, for instance",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 272,
      "topLeftY": 161,
      "bottomRightX": 427,
      "bottomRightY": 197,
      "content": "$$u_{nn'}^{(1)} = \\sum_i \\zeta_i \\int \\overline{\\phi_{n'}^{(0)}} \\frac{\\partial \\phi_n^{(0)}}{\\partial \\xi_i} \\mathrm{d}x$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 272,
      "topLeftY": 201,
      "bottomRightX": 643,
      "bottomRightY": 239,
      "content": "$$u_{nn'}^{(2)} = \\sum_{ij} \\zeta_i \\zeta_j \\int \\overline{\\phi_{n'}^{(0)}} \\frac{\\partial^2 \\phi_n^{(0)}}{\\partial \\xi_i \\partial \\xi_j} \\mathrm{d}x. \\tag{20}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 248,
      "bottomRightX": 644,
      "bottomRightY": 281,
      "content": "These integrals, in which $\\mathrm{d}x$ denotes the volume element in configuration space, are independent of the orientation of the nuclear system in space, hence independent of the $\\theta_i$; one can thus evaluate them in the principal axis system.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 92,
      "topLeftY": 283,
      "bottomRightX": 507,
      "bottomRightY": 299,
      "content": "If now, $F$ denotes any operator on the $x_i$, we define the $r$th order matrix element of $F$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 303,
      "topLeftY": 308,
      "bottomRightX": 643,
      "bottomRightY": 338,
      "content": "$$\\int \\overline{\\phi_{n'}^{(0)}} F \\phi_n^{(r)} \\mathrm{d}x = F_{nn'}^{(r)}. \\tag{21}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 347,
      "bottomRightX": 312,
      "bottomRightY": 361,
      "content": "For $r = 0$ this becomes the usual matrix element",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 285,
      "topLeftY": 369,
      "bottomRightX": 643,
      "bottomRightY": 399,
      "content": "$$F_{nn'}^{(0)} = F_{nn'} = \\int \\overline{\\phi_{n'}^{(0)}} F \\phi_n^{(0)} \\mathrm{d}x. \\tag{22}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 409,
      "bottomRightX": 172,
      "bottomRightY": 424,
      "content": "In general, by (19),",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 306,
      "topLeftY": 422,
      "bottomRightX": 643,
      "bottomRightY": 450,
      "content": "$$F_{nn'}^{(r)} = \\sum_{n''} u_{nn''}^{(r)} F_{n''n'}. \\tag{23}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 457,
      "bottomRightX": 177,
      "bottomRightY": 471,
      "content": "Using (15) for $\\kappa = 0$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 274,
      "topLeftY": 471,
      "bottomRightX": 643,
      "bottomRightY": 491,
      "content": "$$(H_0^{(0)} - V_n^{(0)})_{nn'}^{(r)} = u_{nn'}^{(r)} (V_{n'}^{(0)} - V_n^{(0)}). \\tag{24}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 498,
      "bottomRightX": 489,
      "bottomRightY": 514,
      "content": "Furthermore, we obtain by substituting (16) and (18) in (15), the following identities:",
